// ---- explog cluster oracle (added for the exp/log family) ----
//
// Same construction as the trig/pow maps above: correctly-rounded (mpmath,
// 400-bit) double reference for the true function at each exact input. This is
// required not only for accuracy but for correctness on amd64/Rosetta, where
// Go's own Frexp-based math.Log/Log10 return a wrong value for tiny subnormal
// inputs (e.g. math.Log(5e-324) yields -709.09 instead of -744.44) — so Go
// cannot be the reference. exp/exp2/expm1 span the whole real line (overflow ->
// +Inf); the log family is present only for in-domain inputs (x>0, or x>-1 for
// log1p) so out-of-domain/special inputs fall back to Go's math, which returns
// the exact -Inf/NaN there.

